1. WHAT DOES THIS LICENSE ALLOW?
   - Freedom to Study & Run: You can clone, study, test, and run this DSP voice
     verification system in MATLAB, GNU Octave, or your own environment.
   - Freedom to Modify: You are permitted to fork, refactor, add new DSP filters,
     or adapt the feature extraction pipeline (MFCC, CMVN, GMM-UBM, DTW).
   - Freedom to Distribute: You may share your modified versions or incorporate
     them into non-commercial or commercial tools, provided the copyright notice
     and this license remain intact.

2. WHAT ARE YOUR OBLIGATIONS?
   - Attribution: You MUST preserve the original copyright notice crediting
     S M Sindid Islam Mahodi and co-authors in any copy or substantial portion.
   - Academic Citation: If you use this software, datasets, algorithms, or
     architecture in coursework, research, technical reports, or publications,
     please cite this repository as follows:
     
     Mahodi, S. M. S. I., Khan, S. Z., Morshed, S. I., & Rohan, A. A. (2026).
     Voice-Based Meal Verification System for Hall Dining (Version 4.1.4 Final)
     [Computer software]. Bangladesh University of Engineering and Technology (BUET).

3. BIOMETRIC DATA & ETHICS NOTICE:
   - For student privacy and security, biometric voice samples of non-consenting
     third-party classmates have been strictly removed from this repository.
   - The included voice takes belong exclusively to the contributing project authors
     who consented to provide sample recordings for functional reproducibility.
   - These voice recordings may NOT be used to train malicious deepfake models or
     impersonation attacks against the authors.

